  "family": "continuity",
  "about": "Antimeridian continuity and pole handling: the two properties an unwrapped ring has to keep. A ring never jumps a seam — consecutive points stay less than half a world apart — and its closing point joins the loop in the frame the walk ended in, which for a polar face is a whole world of longitude away from where it began. poleContained names the pole a cell circles, so the adapters can close the loop along the picture's own edge.",
